{
  "analysis": "Starting fresh. I need to examine the music excerpt in /app/Harmony.pdf and understand the task - complete a four-part (SATB) harmonization in Bach chorale style with Roman numeral annotations as <harmony> elements in MusicXML.",
  "plan": "First, let me explore the /app directory and view the PDF to understand what I'm working with.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /app/\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "file /app/Harmony.pdf\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The /app directory contains only Harmony.pdf (9012 bytes). I need to examine the PDF to understand the music excerpt. The `file` command isn't available, so I'll try other tools.",
  "plan": "Check available tools for PDF rendering/extraction (pdftoppm, pdf2image, python, etc.) and view the PDF content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which python3 pdftoppm pdf2image convert gs qpdf mutool 2>/dev/null; echo '---done---'\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings /app/Harmony.pdf | head -50\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Only python3 is available. No pdftoppm, no PDF tools. I'll check Python libraries for PDF reading and see if I can install anything via pip.",
  "plan": "Check installed Python packages for PDF processing, and try pip to install pdf2image/pypdf if possible.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import sys; print(sys.version)\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import pypdf; print('pypdf ok')\" 2>&1; python3 -c \"import PyPDF2; print('PyPDF2 ok')\" 2>&1; python3 -c \"import pdf2image; print('pdf2image ok')\" 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip list 2>/dev/null | head -40\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Only minimal Python packages are installed. Let me try installing pypdf or pdf2image via pip (may need network), and also inspect the raw PDF structure to understand what it contains.",
  "plan": "Try pip install pypdf. Also examine the raw PDF bytes to see if it's a standard PDF with extractable content (maybe it has text/annotations embedded).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip install pypdf 2>&1 | tail -5\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -c 200 /app/Harmony.pdf | od -c | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "It's a real PDF with content streams, images, and fonts. pypdf installed successfully. Let me extract the text content from the PDF to understand the music excerpt.",
  "plan": "Use pypdf to extract text from the PDF. This should reveal the notes, clefs, and any existing annotations.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import pypdf; r=pypdf.PdfReader('/app/Harmony.pdf'); [print(repr(r.pages[i].extract_text())) for i in range(len(r.pages))]\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import pypdf; r=pypdf.PdfReader('/app/Harmony.pdf'); print('pages', len(r.pages)); [print(r.pages[i].mediabox) for i in range(len(r.pages))]\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Shell quoting issues with the inline Python. Let me write a proper script file instead to avoid escaping problems.",
  "plan": "Create a Python script that extracts text and examines the PDF structure properly.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /tmp/examine.py << 'EOF'
import pypdf
r = pypdf.PdfReader('/app/Harmony.pdf')
print('pages:', len(r.pages))
for i in range(len(r.pages)):
    print('--- page', i, '---')
    try:
        t = r.pages[i].extract_text()
        print('TEXT:', repr(t))
    except Exception as e:
        print('extract error:', e)
EOF
python3 /tmp/examine.py
",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The PDF text only shows 'Harmony\\nPiano\\n5' - the title. The actual musical notation is rendered as images (/ImageB, /ImageC in the PDF resources). The melody is an image. I need to extract the images and analyze them.",
  "plan": "Extract the images from the PDF and save them so I can analyze the musical notation. Let me write a script to pull out the image data.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /tmp/extract_img.py << 'EOF'\nimport pypdf\nr = pypdf.PdfReader('/app/Harmony.pdf')\npage = r.pages[0]\nres = page.get_resources()\nprint('Resources:', res)\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/extract_img.py 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Need Pillow for image extraction. Let me install it.",
  "plan": "Install Pillow, then extract images from the PDF.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pip install Pillow 2>&1 | tail -2\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 /tmp/extract_img.py 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The ProcSet references ImageB, ImageC, ImageI. Let me find the actual XObject definitions in the PDF by scanning for /Type /XObject entries. Let me look at the content stream and the full raw PDF.",
  "plan": "Scan the raw PDF for XObject definitions and extract the image streams manually.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"XObject\\|/Type\\|/Filter\\|/Width\\|/Height\\|/ColorSpace\\|/BitsPerComponent\" /app/Harmony.pdf | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - << 'EOF'\nwith open('/app/Harmony.pdf','rb') as f:\n    data = f.read()\nprint('total bytes:', len(data))\n# find xobject positions\nimport re\nfor m in re.finditer(rb'\\d+ 0 obj\\n<<', data):\n    print('obj at', m.start(), m.group().decode())\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "There are objects at offsets 5828, 5903, 7275, 7528 which are likely the image XObjects. Let me extract and examine those regions.",
  "plan": "Extract the regions of the PDF around those offsets to see the image object definitions and their streams.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - << 'EOF'\nwith open('/app/Harmony.pdf','rb') as f:\n    data = f.read()\nprint('=== obj 9 (5828) ===')\nprint(data[5800:6050])\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
